usb_host_uac: report a disconnect even when the close fails

_uac_host_device_disconnected() closes each interface of the device that
went and then tells the user (UAC_HOST_DRIVER_EVENT_DISCONNECTED).  The
close waits for the interface's lock.  A task that holds it across a
control transfer of that device (volume, mute, start, stop) waits for the
transfer's completion, which only this task, the one running the
disconnect, can deliver: both wait DEFAULT_CTRL_XFER_TIMEOUT_MS.  When the
close gives up first, UAC_RETURN_ON_ERROR leaves the function: the user is
never told, the interface stays "open" and the device's other interfaces
are not handled.  The event is now sent whatever the close returns; the
user's own uac_host_device_close() after it releases what was left.

With NDEBUG the assert on the device lookup is gone, and a device that is
not in the list was dereferenced as NULL; the function returns instead.

Applies to espressif/esp-usb 9abfde7ac1723335430474f378976da2d1f68c01.
---
--- a/host/class/uac/usb_host_uac/uac_host.c
+++ b/host/class/uac/usb_host_uac/uac_host.c
@@ -1080,6 +1080,9 @@
     uac_device_t *uac_device = get_uac_device_by_handle(dev_hdl);
     // Device should be in the list
     assert(uac_device);
+    if (uac_device == NULL) {
+        return ESP_ERR_NOT_FOUND;
+    }
 
     UAC_ENTER_CRITICAL();
     uac_iface_t *uac_iface = STAILQ_FIRST(&s_uac_driver->uac_ifaces_tailq);
@@ -1088,8 +1091,14 @@
         UAC_EXIT_CRITICAL();
         if (uac_iface->parent && (uac_iface->parent->addr == uac_device->addr)) {
             uac_iface->flags |= FLAG_INTERFACE_WAIT_USER_DELETE;
-            UAC_RETURN_ON_ERROR(uac_host_device_close(uac_iface), "Unable to close device");
-            UAC_RETURN_ON_ERROR(uac_host_interface_shutdown(uac_iface), "Unable to shutdown interface");
+            // A close that fails (the interface is locked by a task that waits for a
+            // control transfer of the device that is gone) must not keep the event
+            // from the user and from the device's other interfaces: the user's own
+            // close, after the event, releases what this one could not
+            if (uac_host_device_close(uac_iface) != ESP_OK) {
+                ESP_LOGW(TAG, "Unable to close device, the user is notified anyway");
+            }
+            uac_host_interface_shutdown(uac_iface);
         }
         UAC_ENTER_CRITICAL();
         uac_iface = next_iface;
